nding requirement from FIN-212 and the nightly test\nexpectations in tests/test_money.py.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Change committed. Starting CI on the branch now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QR766sx1gVHtcYiaZvVK8E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012meUnnEK6LvRpCPtdiUhxn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Opening the pull request against main and requesting alex as reviewer.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MqKUnKCN8thUiGQ4oQJQDa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 requires banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), and the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` expect it. This caused the nightly build failure.\n\n## Change\n- Switch the rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in `src/money.py`.\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: **passed**.\n- `test_half_even` checks 2.675 -> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66, which are the half-even results.\n\nRef: FIN-212", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but the response lists no reviewers, so I'll explicitly request alex's review.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XGsBwbjzZhM3rHChykfwVA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and the change is up for review as PR #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 and the test expect banker's rounding.\n- **Change:** Switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **Review:** The PR was opened with an empty reviewer list at first, so I requested alex's review separately and the response confirmed it.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}